    "calendar": "All machines start at cycle 1 on day 0 and run CYCLES_PER_DAY cycles a day (the Phase 2 replay convention). A machine fails when it completes cycle L (its true failure point, RUL 0). It runs degraded (speed loss, more scrap) in its last 20 cycles, i.e. while its TRUE remaining life is < 20.",
    "service_timing": "A service booked for day d happens at the start of day d, before that day's cycles run.",
    "after_data_ends": "NASA test files stop before failure. After a machine's last reading the predictive policy has no new data, so it keeps using its last forecast, aged by one cycle per cycle run.",
    "crew_limit": "Only the predictive policy is crew-limited (as in the guide). Run-to-failure and fixed-interval services are not, which favours the two baselines.",
    "work_orders": "A booked service is kept (no re-planning of booked orders). An engine with an open order is not re-booked. If it fails before its service day, that is an unplanned failure and the order is cancelled. Flagged engines left unserved are retried the next day.",
    "rounding": "rul_low is floored to whole cycles before scheduling (the guide's int()); flooring is conservative."
